The following are instructions for how to analyze microscopy images of 2D cell cultures constitutively expressing GFP as seen in publication XXXX for fold change and cell morphology

Before starting:
-Cells of interest MUST have a fluorescent marker expressed throughout the entire cell
-Microscopy images must be taken at 10X magnification
-Cell Profiler must be installed
  -Install available here: https://cellprofiler.org/releases
-Matlab must be installed
-If analyzing multiple images at once is desired, each image must be saved as an individual tiff 

Running Analysis
1. Run Stiffness_Pipeline.cpproj
2. Run QC_Images.m
3. Run Stiffness_Datasort.m
